1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP07 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:07,190
(Behind-the-Scenes)
This is...

4
00:00:08,030 --> 00:00:08,910
A boarding pass.

5
00:00:09,430 --> 00:00:10,140
You got yours?

6
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:10,830
Yep.

7
00:00:11,060 --> 00:00:12,300
(Red ticket)

8
00:00:12,590 --> 00:00:14,860
Go fall in love.

9
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:15,460
Fall in love.

10
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,300
Go fall in love.

11
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:20,910
Fall in love.

12
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:22,910
(Laughs)

13
00:00:22,910 --> 00:00:23,710
All right,

14
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:25,660
let's get one together.

15
00:00:25,870 --> 00:00:26,710
Come on.

16
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:27,590
Let's do it.

17
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:34,580
(Leans in)

18
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:38,030
Sorry!

19
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:38,790
That's the first one.

20
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:40,340
Okay.

21
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:41,620
(I'm sorry!)

22
00:00:41,710 --> 00:00:42,860
This one's great.

23
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,110
Yeah, looks good.

24
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:44,980
Put that away.

25
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:45,820
Let's keep it.

26
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:46,940
Yeah, for the memories.

27
00:00:47,660 --> 00:00:48,460
Here we go.

28
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:49,260
(One more)

29
00:00:49,940 --> 00:00:50,980
(Puts an arm around him)

30
00:00:54,990 --> 00:00:56,190
That one's going to be good.

31
00:00:56,630 --> 00:00:57,670
One for you, and one for me.

32
00:00:57,990 --> 00:00:58,470
Sure.

33
00:00:58,860 --> 00:00:59,830
Can you sit here?

34
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:00,670
I'll get one of you.

35
00:01:00,940 --> 00:01:01,460
Okay.

36
00:01:01,580 --> 00:01:02,460
Three.

37
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:03,420
Two.

38
00:01:03,420 --> 00:01:03,940
One.

39
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:05,710
Hope it's straight.

40
00:01:07,070 --> 00:01:08,110
I'm sure it is.

41
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:10,350
Looks good.

42
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:11,750
(Laughs)

43
00:01:11,750 --> 00:01:12,630
Let me get one of you.

44
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:13,420
Okay.

45
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:14,300
Ready?

46
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:15,020
One.

47
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:16,820
Two.

48
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:17,260
Three.

49
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:20,580
Looks good.

50
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:27,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

51
00:01:27,180 --> 00:01:28,780
(Checking the Polaroids)

52
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:31,070
Okay.

53
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:32,620
I was about to lie down.

54
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:33,340
Go ahead.

55
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:34,870
Let me see.

56
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:38,350
The colors are coming through now.

57
00:01:39,310 --> 00:01:40,670
This one is so pretty.

58
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:43,300
I should've posed more gracefully.

59
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:44,830
I looked graceful, though.

60
00:01:45,020 --> 00:01:46,380
(Joking)

61
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:47,660
(Smacks him)

62
00:01:50,470 --> 00:01:51,830
Your eyes look so big.

63
00:01:51,830 --> 00:01:52,550
(Complimenting her)

64
00:01:52,550 --> 00:01:53,350
Of course.

65
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:56,150
I'm coming.

66
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,100
Wait for me.

67
00:01:58,190 --> 00:01:59,230
Ready?

68
00:01:59,230 --> 00:02:00,220
Let me try this new pack of film.

69
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:00,820
Hold on.

70
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:02,150
Get a solo shot of him.

71
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:02,790
That should work.

72
00:02:02,790 --> 00:02:03,550
Frame him up.

73
00:02:04,310 --> 00:02:04,990
All right.

74
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:06,470
Just focus on him.

75
00:02:06,950 --> 00:02:07,620
Quick, get ready

76
00:02:07,620 --> 00:02:08,110
and pose.

77
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:09,340
Just get my profile.

78
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:10,510
Profile shots are safer.

79
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:15,550
No smile?

80
00:02:17,580 --> 00:02:19,700
Three, two, one.

81
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:20,620
Okay, don't smile.

82
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,670
Don't smile.

83
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:24,270
Let's trust it one more time.

84
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:26,660
I'll give it one more chance.

85
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:28,380
You can compare them.

86
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:31,100
Who took this?

87
00:02:31,100 --> 00:02:32,750
Fang.

88
00:02:33,190 --> 00:02:34,190
So nice.

89
00:02:34,230 --> 00:02:36,070
(Joking)
I still like mine better.

90
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:36,750
Really?

91
00:02:37,670 --> 00:02:38,270
Let me check yours.

92
00:02:38,270 --> 00:02:39,550
It's still...

93
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:40,180
(Pauses)

94
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:41,940
(Purses lips)

95
00:02:42,430 --> 00:02:43,450
This one came out really good.

96
00:02:43,450 --> 00:02:44,340
(Still admiring Fang's work)

97
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:46,260
(Shakes it)

98
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:47,780
(Checks again)

99
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:50,150
Put it in my pocket for a bit.

100
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:50,470
Yours...

101
00:02:50,470 --> 00:02:51,110
You know mine just

102
00:02:51,110 --> 00:02:51,870
takes longer.

103
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:54,300
It's slower than yours.

104
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:56,500
It's okay.

105
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:57,550
We know.

106
00:02:57,710 --> 00:02:58,910
(Reassuring)
We all know.

107
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:02,620
(One more)

108
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:03,950
He's going for another one.

109
00:03:05,300 --> 00:03:06,030
Another one?

110
00:03:06,030 --> 00:03:07,430
This'll be good. Ready?

111
00:03:07,430 --> 00:03:09,580
Three, two, one.

112
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:11,580
It wasn't on.

113
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:14,030
All that posing for nothing.

114
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:15,510
The battery died again.

115
00:03:18,860 --> 00:03:20,710
It finally gave up.

116
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:23,990
He's such a goofball, isn't he?

117
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:31,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

118
00:03:32,210 --> 00:03:33,400
(Behind-the-Scenes)
I'll get a picture of you two.

119
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:34,020
Thanks.

120
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:37,070
Full-body or something closer?

121
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,260
(Waist-up shot)
Let's do a waist-up shot.

122
00:03:40,260 --> 00:03:41,300
"A wifed-up shot".

123
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:42,700
A wifed-up shot?

124
00:03:42,950 --> 00:03:44,340
A wifed-up shot?

125
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:46,820
A wifed-up shot.

126
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,430
A wifed-up...

127
00:03:49,710 --> 00:03:50,300
Okay!

128
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:53,870
All right, wedding photo it is.

129
00:03:55,030 --> 00:03:56,340
I'm kidding.

130
00:03:56,340 --> 00:03:57,020
A wifed-up shot.

131
00:03:57,020 --> 00:03:58,300
Okay, a wifed-up shot.

132
00:04:00,390 --> 00:04:01,470
Nice.

133
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,140
(Admiring the photo)

134
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:06,460
Let me get one of you.

135
00:04:06,460 --> 00:04:07,900
Want to take one together?

136
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:08,180
Sure.

137
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:09,020
Okay! Let's do one.

138
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:09,500
Okay.

139
00:04:09,500 --> 00:04:10,470
Let's do it, Yu Yang.

140
00:04:11,030 --> 00:04:12,510
I'll take it. Let's go.

141
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:15,270
Didn't we take one here yesterday?

142
00:04:15,270 --> 00:04:17,660
Maybe we should try... a different spot.

143
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:18,100
Sure.

144
00:04:18,100 --> 00:04:19,390
Let's switch it up.

145
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:21,510
Let's find another spot.

146
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:23,190
Let's stand over here.

147
00:04:23,190 --> 00:04:24,990
Should we hold hands?

148
00:04:24,990 --> 00:04:27,260
Sure. We can stand here and hold hands.

149
00:04:27,870 --> 00:04:29,300
Want to hold hands?

150
00:04:29,950 --> 00:04:30,950
Let's just hug.

151
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:32,500
(Hugs)
Then I want a hug too.

152
00:04:32,820 --> 00:04:34,390
Then I want a hug too.

153
00:04:35,070 --> 00:04:35,750
It's okay.

154
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:36,580
(Teasing)

155
00:04:37,870 --> 00:04:39,150
What was that?

156
00:04:39,150 --> 00:04:40,950
Yu Yang is heartbroken.

157
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:45,300
One, two...

158
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:47,500
Three.

159
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:48,700
Got it.

160
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:51,140
A wifed-up shot.

161
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:52,190
Our wifed-up shot.

162
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:53,550
Now we have one too.

163
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:59,780
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

164
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:01,340
(Behind-the-Scenes)

165
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:03,470
Today, Yu Yang and I

166
00:05:04,350 --> 00:05:05,350
were on the climbing wall.

167
00:05:06,350 --> 00:05:07,680
We had to jump down from the top.

168
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,110
- Climb up, then jump down.
- Jump down?

169
00:05:14,630 --> 00:05:15,870
I did it so many times.

170
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:17,980
(Concerned)
Yeah.

171
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:19,220
You hit your leg?

172
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,470
You hurt your leg?

173
00:05:21,470 --> 00:05:22,830
Just a little. I'm fine.

174
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:26,310
You did that over and over?

175
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:28,270
Climb up, then jump down?

176
00:05:28,270 --> 00:05:30,430
Yeah. That's why my hair's a mess.

177
00:05:34,110 --> 00:05:35,830
Too bad. I missed it.

178
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,590
I can do it again later.

179
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:39,390
Again?

180
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,110
Yeah.

181
00:05:40,110 --> 00:05:41,910
Won't that mess up your hair?

182
00:05:41,910 --> 00:05:43,020
It's fine.

183
00:05:43,020 --> 00:05:44,070
I'll just fix it.

184
00:05:44,510 --> 00:05:46,030
Who's going to fix it? You?

185
00:05:46,670 --> 00:05:47,750
Getting pretty good,

186
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:48,950
huh?

187
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:52,500
(Look at each other)

188
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:57,540
So handsome.

189
00:05:58,550 --> 00:05:59,190
So handsome.

190
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:07,260
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

191
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,620
(Behind-the-Scenes)

192
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,390
Want any more?

193
00:06:10,070 --> 00:06:11,430
You can finish this.

194
00:06:12,190 --> 00:06:12,910
You have it.

195
00:06:12,910 --> 00:06:13,550
Me?

196
00:06:13,910 --> 00:06:15,220
(Immediately agrees)
Okay, I'll have one.

197
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:16,260
The apple's...

198
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:17,870
Yeah, it's better. Want some?

199
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:18,380
Sure.

200
00:06:23,110 --> 00:06:24,230
This is actually pretty good.

201
00:06:26,020 --> 00:06:27,140
(In sync)

202
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:34,750
Want some?

203
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:36,150
No, you have it.

204
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:37,540
It's just fruit.

205
00:06:37,540 --> 00:06:38,270
Huh? Me?

206
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:40,780
Finish these up.

207
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,150
Finish these up.

208
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:43,620
Look.

209
00:06:43,620 --> 00:06:45,060
We both have one left.

210
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:45,940
Yeah, one each.

211
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:48,230
Pick one.

212
00:06:51,470 --> 00:06:52,380
You pick. I'm good.

213
00:06:52,380 --> 00:06:53,230
Don't you like this?

214
00:06:53,230 --> 00:06:54,300
Then I'll eat this one.

215
00:06:54,790 --> 00:06:55,830
Have them both.

216
00:07:00,670 --> 00:07:02,030
Okay, I'll finish this one too.

217
00:07:07,660 --> 00:07:08,820
(Continues cleaning up)

218
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:16,500
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

219
00:07:16,990 --> 00:07:18,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Oh, you came down.

220
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:18,910
Yeah.

221
00:07:18,910 --> 00:07:20,140
I'll take your bottle.

222
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:20,950
Okay.

223
00:07:25,390 --> 00:07:26,420
Looks good.

224
00:07:26,830 --> 00:07:28,020
Where's your blanket?

225
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,180
Where is it?

226
00:07:29,710 --> 00:07:30,500
Cold?

227
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,310
I'm okay.

228
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:34,060
(Takes off his jacket)

229
00:07:34,190 --> 00:07:35,940
Guess you'll have to wear mine.

230
00:07:36,220 --> 00:07:37,910
Guess you'll have to wear mine.

231
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:39,260
You...

232
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:44,020
(Helps her)

233
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:50,540
(Hands it over)

234
00:07:51,110 --> 00:07:52,070
Looks good.

235
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:55,620
(Fixes collar)
It looks really sharp like this.

236
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:56,830
Really? Like this?

237
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:58,350
Does this really look good?

238
00:07:59,590 --> 00:08:00,460
Why does this

239
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,340
feel a little off on me?

240
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:03,990
Then wear the one I've got on.

241
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:05,390
Are you wearing anything underneath?

242
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:05,910
Nope.

243
00:08:06,270 --> 00:08:07,390
Then never mind.

244
00:08:09,950 --> 00:08:11,700
(Looks)
You look really good.

245
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,180
You're good at posing.

246
00:08:15,180 --> 00:08:16,460
I've got it down now.

247
00:08:16,460 --> 00:08:17,540
(Hands on hips)
I'll do that next time.

248
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:18,550
Then I'll do this.

249
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:19,380
(Teasing)

250
00:08:22,990 --> 00:08:23,830
Why do I look...

251
00:08:24,140 --> 00:08:24,940
(Leans closer)
What?

252
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:26,420
So pale.

253
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:27,180
Too pale?

254
00:08:27,180 --> 00:08:27,540
Not really.

255
00:08:27,540 --> 00:08:29,140
I look kind of washed out.

256
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,260
How rosy do you want to look?

257
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,150
(Perfect)
You look great.

258
00:08:33,910 --> 00:08:36,070
Why does your face look so slim today?

259
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:38,390
But not from this angle.

260
00:08:39,270 --> 00:08:39,700
I know.

261
00:08:39,700 --> 00:08:41,180
It's only when you aren't smiling.

262
00:08:41,180 --> 00:08:41,980
Yeah.

263
00:08:42,950 --> 00:08:44,180
Then I won't smile next time.

264
00:08:44,180 --> 00:08:46,180
You want hollow cheeks too?

265
00:08:46,180 --> 00:08:47,270
Mine don't do that.

266
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,700
(Look at each other)

267
00:08:52,340 --> 00:08:54,140
(Laughs)

268
00:08:54,140 --> 00:08:55,870
My face is just rounder.

269
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:57,190
I've got fuller cheeks.

270
00:08:57,470 --> 00:08:58,420
You can't pinch them right now.

271
00:08:58,420 --> 00:08:59,430
I've got makeup on.

272
00:09:01,870 --> 00:09:02,830
I know.

273
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:09,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

274
00:09:10,430 --> 00:09:11,750
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Let's open these up.

275
00:09:12,430 --> 00:09:13,390
(Opening the Polaroids)
You do mine?

276
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:14,620
Yeah.

277
00:09:14,620 --> 00:09:14,950
How is it?

278
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,700
(Surprised)

279
00:09:20,830 --> 00:09:22,100
Guess where this is.

280
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:22,990
Where?

281
00:09:24,150 --> 00:09:26,270
This is from my place,

282
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:27,350
right outside my window.

283
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:30,350
That rainy view you told me about?

284
00:09:30,550 --> 00:09:31,830
Do you like rainy days?

285
00:09:32,750 --> 00:09:33,950
I like staying in

286
00:09:33,950 --> 00:09:34,550
when it rains.

287
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:36,950
I like being at home

288
00:09:36,950 --> 00:09:38,390
with the window open.

289
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:41,190
My balcony kind of wraps around.

290
00:09:41,190 --> 00:09:42,990
When it rains, I leave the window open

291
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:44,830
and just sit there.

292
00:09:45,380 --> 00:09:46,260
(Nods)

293
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:48,100
(Looks closely)

294
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,740
Whenever I've got nothing to do,

295
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:52,980
I'll sit by the window
and watch this tree.

296
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:56,030
So I took a picture.

297
00:09:57,990 --> 00:09:59,750
I wanted to show you...

298
00:10:00,510 --> 00:10:01,990
How it changes with the seasons?

299
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:03,110
Just watching

300
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:04,190
it change all year long.

301
00:10:06,470 --> 00:10:07,020
I'll give it to you.

302
00:10:07,020 --> 00:10:07,700
Is that okay?

303
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:08,460
Of course.

304
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:13,460
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

305
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:19,660
(Behind-the-Scenes)

306
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,430
Back when I was heavier,

307
00:10:22,350 --> 00:10:23,750
you couldn't even see my ears
from the front.

308
00:10:24,390 --> 00:10:25,230
Let me see.

309
00:10:26,020 --> 00:10:27,540
(Moves closer)

310
00:10:28,750 --> 00:10:30,630
I can see them well now.

311
00:10:31,950 --> 00:10:32,630
When was that?

312
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,540
Senior year.

313
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:34,390
Senior year?

314
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:35,590
So you got thinner in college?

315
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,860
Not right away.

316
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:40,150
It was pretty gradual.

317
00:10:41,670 --> 00:10:44,230
So college was when you realized

318
00:10:44,230 --> 00:10:45,550
you were handsome

319
00:10:45,550 --> 00:10:46,390
(Teasing)
and decided to slim down?

320
00:10:47,430 --> 00:10:49,750
I just wondered
what I'd look like if I were thinner.

321
00:10:50,110 --> 00:10:51,910
So I got curious and lost some weight.

322
00:10:52,510 --> 00:10:54,270
I was also heavier
during my senior year.

323
00:10:54,270 --> 00:10:56,870
But you're way taller than me.

324
00:10:57,390 --> 00:10:58,660
You've got a bigger frame too.

325
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:00,590
I'm not that much taller.

326
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:02,630
Aren't you like 20 cm taller?

327
00:11:03,430 --> 00:11:06,010
That's the perfect height difference.

328
00:11:06,010 --> 00:11:06,940
(Perfect height difference)

329
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:11,420
Isn't it?

330
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:12,300
It is.

331
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:13,740
It is.

332
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:22,860
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

333
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,140
(Behind-the-Scenes)

334
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:26,310
Is that a plane?

335
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:27,510
I've been watching it for a while.

336
00:11:27,510 --> 00:11:28,950
I thought it was a kite.

337
00:11:29,910 --> 00:11:31,870
A kite wouldn't be that bright.

338
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:37,270
It's a plane. See it blinking?

339
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:41,470
Well, it's definitely not a UFO.

340
00:11:42,310 --> 00:11:43,790
Do you believe in aliens?

341
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,510
I do. You?

342
00:11:45,510 --> 00:11:46,710
Me too.

343
00:11:47,470 --> 00:11:49,150
Is this hard to set up?

344
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:50,780
Yeah.

345
00:11:52,110 --> 00:11:55,150
Maybe not. It calibrates itself.

346
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,340
This...

347
00:12:02,070 --> 00:12:03,270
That's so smart.

348
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:10,350
Maria, you really know your stuff.

349
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:12,940
Can you see it?

350
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:15,620
I think I can see something
really faint.

351
00:12:16,380 --> 00:12:16,940
There is.

352
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:17,710
Really?

353
00:12:17,710 --> 00:12:18,830
I think so.

354
00:12:21,430 --> 00:12:22,750
See? We needed the genius.

355
00:12:23,230 --> 00:12:24,630
Oh, stop it.

356
00:12:26,380 --> 00:12:31,340
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

357
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:33,830
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Yu Yang, can you help me?

358
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:35,860
Sure. What do you need?

359
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,830
(Heating shrink plastic)
I need to shrink this down.

360
00:12:37,830 --> 00:12:38,460
Okay.

361
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:41,420
(Hand-drawn portrait of Cui Kaiyi)

362
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,550
(Points)
You drew this?

363
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:46,750
Yeah, a couple of days ago.

364
00:12:47,510 --> 00:12:48,710
Once it shrinks,

365
00:12:48,710 --> 00:12:51,030
it might start curling up.

366
00:12:51,030 --> 00:12:52,110
So I'll use this to...

367
00:12:52,110 --> 00:12:54,150
Use this to flatten it back out gently.

368
00:12:54,150 --> 00:12:55,140
Got it.

369
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:55,740
Here.

370
00:12:58,230 --> 00:12:59,590
Let's warm it up first.

371
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:00,980
Here we go.

372
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:05,380
(Shrinking)

373
00:13:06,310 --> 00:13:07,670
That looks really good.

374
00:13:07,940 --> 00:13:09,060
Okay, that's good.

375
00:13:09,990 --> 00:13:11,830
I'll just adjust it a little by hand.

376
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:12,830
Careful, it's hot.

377
00:13:12,830 --> 00:13:13,670
It's fine.

378
00:13:14,230 --> 00:13:16,750
Okay, perfect.

379
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:18,870
That looks so good.

380
00:13:19,230 --> 00:13:21,580
And the color came out just right.

381
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:22,460
Really?

382
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:25,300
Press it down.

383
00:13:28,430 --> 00:13:29,550
Crank up the heat.

384
00:13:31,430 --> 00:13:31,940
Perfect.

385
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:32,780
Thanks.

386
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:33,670
No problem.

387
00:13:33,830 --> 00:13:35,830
It's so tiny now.

388
00:13:38,830 --> 00:13:40,270
That's so cute.

389
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:42,710
Mini Kaiyi.

390
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:45,910
This is actually

391
00:13:45,910 --> 00:13:48,630
what she wore on our first date,

392
00:13:49,630 --> 00:13:51,470
when we went to the sports field.

393
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:52,740
(Looks closely)

394
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:56,670
Okay, perfect.

395
00:13:59,700 --> 00:14:04,660
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

396
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:07,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)

397
00:14:07,020 --> 00:14:08,590
Which one do you like

398
00:14:09,510 --> 00:14:11,470
out of these three colors?

399
00:14:11,470 --> 00:14:12,260
White,

400
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:12,660
purple,

401
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:13,710
or pink.

402
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,230
Which one's purple?

403
00:14:17,750 --> 00:14:19,350
The one standing up, right?

404
00:14:19,350 --> 00:14:20,150
Let me see.

405
00:14:28,510 --> 00:14:29,710
This is the purple one.

406
00:14:31,990 --> 00:14:32,910
I'll sit over here.

407
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:37,750
I think I like white.

408
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:39,980
(Makes a note)

409
00:14:40,510 --> 00:14:41,230
What about you?

410
00:14:41,230 --> 00:14:42,390
That one. For sure.

411
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:43,150
Really?

412
00:14:43,150 --> 00:14:43,950
Yeah.

413
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:46,070
Why white?

414
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:50,630
Those two are a little too bright.

415
00:14:52,070 --> 00:14:52,950
White looks cleaner?

416
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:05,180
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

417
00:15:05,220 --> 00:15:06,860
(Behind-the-Scenes)

418
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:07,900
This is so embarrassing.

419
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:10,110
We're both crying so much.

420
00:15:11,470 --> 00:15:12,510
Good thing it's raining.

421
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,510
We can just blame it on the rain.

422
00:15:31,310 --> 00:15:32,830
These are our tickets?

423
00:15:32,830 --> 00:15:33,620
Yeah.

424
00:15:33,620 --> 00:15:34,820
(Notices the ticket holder)

425
00:15:35,110 --> 00:15:36,380
We can put them in here.

426
00:15:37,870 --> 00:15:39,030
How does this open?

427
00:15:39,710 --> 00:15:41,030
I think it just clips on.

428
00:15:41,230 --> 00:15:41,820
Like this?

429
00:15:41,820 --> 00:15:43,030
(Puts them in together)
Yeah, that's it.

430
00:15:43,030 --> 00:15:43,670
You're right.

431
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:45,030
Mine is...

432
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:46,620
(Immediately follows)
in my bag.

433
00:15:47,350 --> 00:15:48,630
It's upside down.

434
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:51,180
(Laughs)

435
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:55,870
Okay.

436
00:15:56,590 --> 00:15:57,790
All right, then.

437
00:15:58,030 --> 00:15:59,990
(Picks up gifts)
Let's grab our stuff.

438
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,220
You take the umbrella. I've got this.

439
00:16:03,550 --> 00:16:04,910
(Helps)
I can take this too.

440
00:16:05,550 --> 00:16:06,710
And the flowers?

441
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,140
I'll hold it.

442
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:10,780
(Takes turns with the umbrella)

443
00:16:11,190 --> 00:16:12,030
Look at all this stuff. Gifts,

444
00:16:12,030 --> 00:16:12,940
flowers,

445
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:13,990
and the umbrella.

446
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:18,940
Okay.

447
00:16:19,950 --> 00:16:20,270
Let's go.

448
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:21,580
Come on.

449
00:16:21,580 --> 00:16:22,220
Let's go home.

450
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:22,790
Okay.

451
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:29,580
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

452
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:30,500
(Behind-the-Scenes)

453
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,870
Didn't you say you used to eat udon
all the time

454
00:16:32,870 --> 00:16:33,790
back in school?

455
00:16:33,790 --> 00:16:34,390
Yeah.

456
00:16:34,390 --> 00:16:36,390
I actually had udon for lunch today.

457
00:16:40,630 --> 00:16:41,500
Oops. My bad.

458
00:16:41,500 --> 00:16:42,310
It's okay.

459
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,150
I should've made you

460
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:44,430
Shin Ramyun

461
00:16:44,430 --> 00:16:45,470
with two eggs.

462
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:49,150
What do you usually add to Shin Ramyun?

463
00:16:50,390 --> 00:16:51,300
Eggs.

464
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,110
How many?

465
00:16:52,670 --> 00:16:53,460
Two.

466
00:16:54,110 --> 00:16:55,030
You really...

467
00:16:55,030 --> 00:16:55,750
know what's good.

468
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:56,870
Really like eggs, huh?

469
00:16:57,910 --> 00:16:59,950
I made tomatoes and eggs yesterday.

470
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:01,340
Oh no.

471
00:17:02,110 --> 00:17:03,910
The first time I made it sweet.

472
00:17:04,470 --> 00:17:05,790
I didn't even get to try it.

473
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,190
It's okay.

474
00:17:07,190 --> 00:17:08,660
You can try
the better version next time.

475
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:10,190
I thought it needed
a little more flavor.

476
00:17:10,380 --> 00:17:11,180
Okay.

477
00:17:14,430 --> 00:17:15,590
Let's turn it off

478
00:17:15,590 --> 00:17:16,710
and let it cook a bit.

479
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:17,150
Sure.

480
00:17:17,550 --> 00:17:18,790
How done do you like it?

481
00:17:19,350 --> 00:17:20,870
A little more well-done.

482
00:17:21,190 --> 00:17:22,190
Then turn the heat back on.

483
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:23,660
(Turns the heat back on)

484
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,870
(Joking)
I like mine still mooing.

485
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:36,380
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

486
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,660
(Behind-the-Scenes)

487
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,270
Tomorrow's our last day here.

488
00:17:40,510 --> 00:17:42,310
That went by so fast.

489
00:17:42,310 --> 00:17:42,980
So fast!

490
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:45,430
It feels like we just got here.

491
00:17:46,900 --> 00:17:48,190
I hope we get a happy ending.

492
00:17:48,190 --> 00:17:48,990
Yeah.

493
00:17:48,990 --> 00:17:49,830
We will.

494
00:17:51,990 --> 00:17:52,910
I'm heading back in.

495
00:17:53,870 --> 00:17:54,670
Bye.

496
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:02,150
I really want to see

497
00:18:02,430 --> 00:18:04,070
Bohan and Xing finally meet.

498
00:18:04,870 --> 00:18:05,590
Me too.

499
00:18:06,590 --> 00:18:07,310
I can't wait.

500
00:18:07,350 --> 00:18:08,870
Can we watch? Never mind.

501
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:10,100
They need some time alone.

502
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:11,660
Yeah, let them have their moment.

503
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:12,710
Yeah, just the two of them.

504
00:18:13,630 --> 00:18:14,260
I bet

505
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,550
they've got

506
00:18:16,070 --> 00:18:17,790
a lot to say.

507
00:18:18,510 --> 00:18:20,870
All those messages they've been sending

508
00:18:21,150 --> 00:18:23,590
probably made their feelings even...

509
00:18:23,710 --> 00:18:24,460
Stronger.

510
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:25,870
Yeah, stronger.

511
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:27,630
Writing just feels different.

512
00:18:27,910 --> 00:18:29,950
What you write can feel deeper
than what you say.

513
00:18:30,110 --> 00:18:31,950
Yeah, sometimes you can't even
put it into words.

514
00:18:32,190 --> 00:18:33,550
Exactly. That's how deep it is.

515
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:35,110
You know he's thinking about her.

516
00:18:35,110 --> 00:18:37,030
He thinks about her every day,

517
00:18:37,030 --> 00:18:37,870
and she probably does too.

518
00:18:38,030 --> 00:18:39,550
And they put all of that
into those messages.

519
00:18:40,070 --> 00:18:40,750
That's really romantic.

520
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:41,510
Seriously.

521
00:18:43,340 --> 00:18:48,300
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

522
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:50,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)

523
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,430
I found out that wiggling your ears

524
00:18:51,430 --> 00:18:52,700
uses a nerve by your eyebrows

525
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,380
to control them.

526
00:18:55,390 --> 00:18:56,380
(Asks)
Can you do it?

527
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,100
Nope.

528
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:59,310
I can wiggle my ears too.

529
00:18:59,310 --> 00:19:00,030
You can?

530
00:19:00,420 --> 00:19:01,220
Yeah, you can.

531
00:19:02,470 --> 00:19:04,190
I feel like when I move my eyebrows,

532
00:19:04,190 --> 00:19:05,030
my ears move too.

533
00:19:07,470 --> 00:19:08,510
Hold your brows still.

534
00:19:08,990 --> 00:19:10,670
I guess mine aren't connected.

535
00:19:11,550 --> 00:19:12,190
Really?

536
00:19:13,870 --> 00:19:15,110
(Looks)
Can you wiggle yours?

537
00:19:17,590 --> 00:19:18,550
Bohan, you look so funny.

538
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:20,420
(Looks)

539
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,740
(Wiggles ears)

540
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:25,470
I can do it too.

541
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:26,470
Really?

542
00:19:26,470 --> 00:19:27,350
Not bad, Cui Kaiyi.

543
00:19:27,580 --> 00:19:28,380
Yeah.

544
00:19:29,420 --> 00:19:30,100
He can do it too.

545
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,150
Yeah, I can.

546
00:19:31,510 --> 00:19:32,590
Now do it together.

547
00:19:32,590 --> 00:19:33,150
Look.

548
00:19:35,230 --> 00:19:36,390
Yeah!

549
00:19:36,710 --> 00:19:37,380
Look at you two,

550
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:37,940
totally in sync.

551
00:19:42,510 --> 00:19:43,870
More dumplings, anyone?

552
00:19:44,110 --> 00:19:44,870
Thanks.

553
00:19:45,670 --> 00:19:47,150
There's still some room here.

554
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:48,500
Careful.

555
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:50,630
This seriously
feels like Chinese New Year.

556
00:19:50,910 --> 00:19:51,790
Yeah, it's like a feast.

557
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:53,110
We eat like this every day.

558
00:19:53,110 --> 00:19:53,780
Seriously, every day.

559
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:55,660
All around this tiny little table.

560
00:19:56,780 --> 00:20:01,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

561
00:20:02,070 --> 00:20:03,990
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Come on, let's go pick the menu.

562
00:20:05,140 --> 00:20:05,660
Okay.

563
00:20:06,300 --> 00:20:07,380
What do you want?

564
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:09,430
Which one?

565
00:20:09,430 --> 00:20:09,990
How...

566
00:20:10,670 --> 00:20:11,510
about this one?

567
00:20:11,510 --> 00:20:13,140
(Blazing Romance)

568
00:20:13,350 --> 00:20:14,110
Sure.

569
00:20:14,110 --> 00:20:14,820
(Instant yes)

570
00:20:14,910 --> 00:20:15,790
That sounds good.

571
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:18,150
Then we can cook luosifen

572
00:20:18,150 --> 00:20:19,870
right in the hot pot.

573
00:20:20,350 --> 00:20:21,790
You want luosifen?

574
00:20:21,830 --> 00:20:23,270
Yeah, I like it.

575
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:26,550
Still thinking about luosifen.

576
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:28,110
Okay, let's go with this one.

577
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:29,870
Yeah, we'll get...

578
00:20:33,990 --> 00:20:35,270
the Blazing Romance set.

579
00:20:35,340 --> 00:20:35,900
Okay.

580
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:36,950
Okay.

581
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:38,380
Careful.

582
00:20:38,710 --> 00:20:39,780
I can't.

583
00:20:42,020 --> 00:20:43,180
(Stamps)

584
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:45,980
(Keeps stamping)

585
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:48,740
Okay, that's clear.

586
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:49,820
It's just one circle.

587
00:20:50,190 --> 00:20:51,430
That's much clearer.

588
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:52,820
Let's go.

589
00:20:55,470 --> 00:20:56,950
My hair looks so flat today.

590
00:20:56,950 --> 00:20:57,830
No, it's not.

591
00:20:58,820 --> 00:20:59,660
You look good.

592
00:21:00,670 --> 00:21:02,190
I just fixed it again.

593
00:21:02,190 --> 00:21:04,030
You fixed it again?

594
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:09,580
(Behind-the-Scenes 17)

595
00:21:09,620 --> 00:21:45,100
(Behind-the-Scenes)

596
00:21:45,140 --> 00:21:50,100
(Behind-the-Scenes 18)

597
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:52,510
("Weekend Crush" early access preview)
First time picking mushrooms?

598
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:54,910
Yep, first time ever.

599
00:21:55,310 --> 00:21:56,510
Another first

600
00:21:56,510 --> 00:21:57,350
with me, then.

601
00:22:00,390 --> 00:22:01,350
Slow down a bit.

602
00:22:04,110 --> 00:22:04,750
Tired?

603
00:22:05,030 --> 00:22:06,910
No, I'm just really hot.

604
00:22:06,910 --> 00:22:07,500
It's so hot.

605
00:22:09,790 --> 00:22:11,470
This one's huge. What is it?

606
00:22:11,730 --> 00:22:12,570
I've never seen that before.

607
00:22:13,230 --> 00:22:14,390
Watch the branches.

608
00:22:14,390 --> 00:22:16,070
It's slippery here.

609
00:22:16,070 --> 00:22:17,070
Take it easy.

610
00:22:18,190 --> 00:22:19,150
Where's the scrape?

611
00:22:19,150 --> 00:22:19,910
Here?

612
00:22:20,590 --> 00:22:21,390
Down here too?

613
00:22:21,390 --> 00:22:22,230
That part's fine.

614
00:22:22,710 --> 00:22:24,190
Xing, spray a little more.

615
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:29,870
That planter you bought...

616
00:22:29,870 --> 00:22:32,230
Did you pick it out or make it yourself?

617
00:22:32,230 --> 00:22:33,390
You know what's funny?

618
00:22:33,390 --> 00:22:35,590
It originally

619
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:37,190
didn't have that little star.

620
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:38,420
It just had the river.

621
00:22:38,420 --> 00:22:40,030
So I asked them to add

622
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:41,470
a little star.

623
00:22:42,070 --> 00:22:43,150
It reminded me

624
00:22:43,150 --> 00:22:44,230
of our boating trip.

625
00:22:44,230 --> 00:22:45,030
Yeah.

626
00:22:45,630 --> 00:22:47,150
Xing, we should each make one

627
00:22:47,150 --> 00:22:47,710
for each other.

628
00:22:47,710 --> 00:22:48,110
Sure.

629
00:22:48,110 --> 00:22:48,510
Deal?

630
00:22:48,510 --> 00:22:49,070
Deal.

631
00:22:51,540 --> 00:22:53,460
Yours is probably better.

632
00:22:53,990 --> 00:22:54,820
If mine's bad,

633
00:22:54,820 --> 00:22:56,100
don't...

634
00:22:56,100 --> 00:22:56,750
reject it.

635
00:22:57,190 --> 00:22:58,030
You won't, right?

636
00:22:58,030 --> 00:22:58,590
I won't.

637
00:22:58,590 --> 00:22:59,390
You won't?

638
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:06,230
I can't. My hand won't fit.

639
00:23:06,230 --> 00:23:07,390
Did you get yours in?

640
00:23:07,390 --> 00:23:08,430
Nope.

641
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:13,470
I think I broke a leaf.

642
00:23:13,470 --> 00:23:14,430
It's okay.

643
00:23:15,710 --> 00:23:16,990
Yours looks really good.

644
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:18,830
Yours does too.

645
00:23:21,230 --> 00:23:22,430
This is definitely burnt.

646
00:23:23,430 --> 00:23:25,310
But it looks so good.

647
00:23:25,710 --> 00:23:27,150
That's exactly how I like it.

648
00:23:27,150 --> 00:23:28,990
If it's not charred, I don't want it.

649
00:23:29,390 --> 00:23:30,230
We'll eat it later.

650
00:23:31,060 --> 00:23:32,440
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

651
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:33,630
